@startuml
title The `UInt32` lexeme as a finite automaton (`languages/src/turing.rs:139`)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}

state "START" as S #DCFCE7
state "saw <latex>0</latex>\nboth a decimal digit and\na possible radix prefix" as Z #FEF3C7

state "BINARY" as BIN #DBEAFE {
  state "body\naccepting" as B #DBEAFE
  state "separator\nNOT accepting" as BS #FCE7F3
  B --> BS : `_`
  BS --> B : `[01]`
  B --> B : `[01]`
}

state "OCTAL" as OCT #DBEAFE {
  state "body\naccepting" as O #DBEAFE
  state "separator\nNOT accepting" as OS #FCE7F3
  O --> OS : `_`
  OS --> O : `[0-7]`
  O --> O : `[0-7]`
}

state "HEXADECIMAL" as HEX #DBEAFE {
  state "body\naccepting" as H #DBEAFE
  state "separator\nNOT accepting" as HS #FCE7F3
  H --> HS : `_`
  HS --> H : `[0-9A-Fa-f]`
  H --> H : `[0-9A-Fa-f]`
}

state "DECIMAL" as DEC #DBEAFE {
  state "body\naccepting" as D #DBEAFE
  state "separator\nNOT accepting" as DS #FCE7F3
  D --> DS : `_`
  DS --> D : `[0-9]`
  D --> D : `[0-9]`
}

state "suffix <latex>\mathtt{u32}</latex>\nconsumed" as U #EDE9FE
state "ACCEPT" as A #DCFCE7

[*] --> S
S --> Z : `0`
S --> D : `[1-9]`

Z --> B : `b` then one `[01]`
Z --> O : `o` then one `[0-7]`
Z --> H : `x` then one `[0-9A-Fa-f]`
Z --> D : one more `[0-9]`
Z --> U : `u32`

B --> U : `u32`
O --> U : `u32`
H --> U : `u32`
D --> U : `u32`

U --> A
A --> [*]

note right of BIN
  Every radix lane has the SAME shape, because the source
  pattern repeats the same idiom four times: one digit,
  then any number of *optionally-separated* further digits.
  The separator state is **not** accepting and has **no**
  self-loop, which is exactly why `1_u32` and `1__0u32`
  are rejected. `_1u32` is rejected for the mirror reason:
  START has no `_` edge.
end note

note bottom of U
  The suffix sits OUTSIDE the alternation group in the source
  pattern, so it is mandatory for every radix. That is what keeps
  the surface `q0` unambiguous: `0` alone is not a `UInt32` lexeme,
  so `q0` can only be the nullary constructor `Q0`, never the
  indexed former `Q` applied to a literal.
end note

note bottom of Z
  A leading `0` is genuinely shared: the same character begins the
  decimal literal `0u32` and each of the radix prefixes `0b` / `0o` /
  `0x`. One character of lookahead resolves it, and this is the only
  place in the token class that needs any.
end note

@enduml
